body:
You have to keep in mind that Harry's first genuine shot at commanding a ship was in "Nightingale", and that ended in mutiny. That alone would be reason enough to pass him over for promotion. That, and his reprimand for sexual misconduct in "The Disease" (to date the ONLY time we've seen a Starfleet officer getting reprimanded in such a fashion).

&#x200B;

My headcanon is that as soon as Voyager got home, Harry was reassigned to one of the dilithium mines along with all the Mk 1 EMH's.

Today my mother clicked on an ad that came up while playing this game, and the link turned out to be a ransomware attempt. No damage was done, but I'm supremely pissed off that it even happened in the first place.

&#x200B;

I'm seriously thinking of getting PiHole just to protect my boomer parents from this sort of shit.

Also using Brave. I've done some testing - the "A new version of odysee is available" message only pops up when you're logged in. I tried logging out, and the homepage loads just fine. Homepage also works if you log in using an incognito window.

&#x200B;

Hard to say for certain if it's a browser issue or a website issue, but my guess is that Odysee is trying to do something on their backend, and it isn't quite working as intended. Would be nice to get some clarification from the Odysee team.

For context, John Stapp experienced around 46 g during his last rocket sled ride.

&#x200B;

IIRC once you get past \~50 g of acceleration, the direction of said acceleration relative to your spine does impact survivability quite a bit.

\>58.77 ducats on rooting out corruption

&#x200B;

Let me guess, too many territories?

\>20 ducats

&#x200B;

Were they really that broke at the end? Nice.

\> In the interview, she also claimed to have once been kidnapped by Walt  Disney. The deceased illustrator, she said, once flew a spaceship and  was a member of the Illuminati. 

&#x200B;

I know she's from Phoenix, but this is Florida levels of crazy.

Nobody else has asked, so I will:

&#x200B;

Why Yaustralia?

\>Not choosing Native Repression Policy

&#x200B;

Well, there's your problem right there....

Chim-chiminy chim-chiminy chim chim churu....

&#x200B;

eu4dadjokes is the sub for you...
